# The build context is THIS directory (compose.chain.yml: `context: .`).
#
# Without this, `COPY svc svc` carries the HOST's svc/node_modules into the
# image on top of the symlink farm `bun install` just built there. bun links a
# workspace member's deps as `svc/node_modules/viem -> ../../../node_modules/
# .bun/...` — three levels up, which is the repo root on the host and `/`
# inside the image, where /app/svc/node_modules is only two below /app.
# chain-svc died with `ENOENT reading "/app/svc/node_modules/viem"`.
#
# WHY THIS DID NOT BITE BEFORE THE SPLIT, because the obvious answer is wrong:
# the harness's root .dockerignore says a bare `node_modules`, which matches the
# CONTEXT ROOT ONLY — chain/svc/node_modules was copied into that image too.
# It worked because /app/chain/svc/node_modules is three levels below /app, so
# the same `../../../` landed on the root node_modules by coincidence of DEPTH.
# The move to `context: .` removed one level and the coincidence with it.
#
# So `**/` is the load-bearing part of the first rule, not decoration.
**/node_modules
**/*.log
.env
**/chain.env
.git
# Foundry build output and vendored libraries: not copied by svc/Dockerfile,
# but they are the bulk of a context that would otherwise go to the daemon.
contracts/out
contracts/cache
contracts/broadcast
contracts/lib
